# Inside the Belly (otherAreas 26): the accepted section's 166 / 167 finish.
# FISHING_ENABLE (P6): `setting map.FISHING_ENABLE true` in the header; every section reads xi.settings.map.FISHING_ENABLE == true
# (false in settings/default/map.lua).
# Accepted (a GM), skill 30. A Sekiryu traded: confirmed now, <= 481: 166 (0, the Sekiryu's Liver); the finish gives the
# liver and 1512 gil, completes the quest and adds fame +10 San d'Oria and Bastok. A GM then makes the quest available
# and accepted again; a Zafmlug Bass traded: > 14: 167; the finish gives 15 gil, completes the quest and adds the fame.
# A deliberate change from the Lua (user ruling 2026-11-04, kept Lua bugs): the lookup then runs the completed section's
# finish too (its check holds once completed); the Lua's giveReward reads the cleared fishId (0) and raises on
# fishRewards[0] (Inside_the_Belly.lua:546), the C# gives nothing there.
warning: quests: otherAreas.inside_the_belly: one finish of 166 ran 2 handlers (2/-/onEventFinish:166, 3/-/onEventFinish:166) -- the Lua runs it twice too: its sections' checks at Inside_the_Belly.lua:651 (accepted) and :692 (completed) at lua-at 3cb2f487 hold the finish, and the lookup reads each check after the earlier handlers ran, so the first's completion lets the second match (on Lua it raises)
